title: 'Registrar: schedule code upgrade'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      `pallet-registrar-para::schedule_code_upgrade` asks the relay chain to authorize a validation
      code upgrade for a registered para. Root, the para itself, or its manager while unlocked may
      call it. Only the code hash and length are sent, no deposit is taken, and the answer comes
      back as an event.

      `pallet-registrar-relay` checks the request through `ParachainRegistrar::check_code_upgrade`,
      which now returns a `FailureReason`, and stores the authorization in `PendingCodeUpgrades`,
      replacing any earlier one for that para. Anyone can then upload the matching code with the
      new unsigned, fee-free `apply_authorized_code_upgrade`, which schedules the upgrade and
      reports back to the parachain. Unlike registrations, the authorization expires after the new
      `CodeUpgradeValidPeriod`, which runtimes using the pallet must set.

      `paras_registrar` in `polkadot-runtime-common` implements `check_code_upgrade` and
      `schedule_code_upgrade`, using the new
      `polkadot_runtime_parachains::can_upgrade_validation_code`.

crates:
  - name: registrar-primitives
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: patch
  - name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
    bump: minor
